  "scope": [
    "Freeform sweeps of analytic and equivalent rational arc rails, both refit settings, different radii, translated and rotated planes, reversed traversal and profiles with a normal component.",
    "Every captured surface participates. Full-order join knots preserve all face boundaries and both one-sided limits. Equal V weight rows make V affine. One shared monotone U correspondence for both complete boundary atlases certifies the entire surface image by convexity.",
    "Local derivative projections only propose mapping nodes. The exact rational curve certificate decides acceptance. Proof reuse requires exact equality of both actual surface atlases and complete captured values.",
    "The source minimum-distance witness remains a geometric certificate. Analytic-arc command transport uses a distinct native-parameter policy inferred from public command outputs. Other geometry parameter maps and explicit station scripts are unchanged.",
    "The additional interval and inserted-knot captures are investigation evidence, not claims of complete surface agreement. Face partition, topology, derivatives and UV parameterization are outside the image comparison.",
    "Rail continuity is checked on original source knot tangents, restricted to the swept interval in the original rational chart. No requested stations are snapped. Coincident mapped frame parameters share one transported frame. Seam validation and real corner rejection remain active."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Near-Greville rational multi-span station decisions",
    "Spatial sweep image gap independently certified by surface-distance-validation.json",
    "Closed-rail branch/seam choices and holonomy",
    "Rail miters and remaining Sweep1 options",
    "Full application feature coverage and performance qualification"
